    "rich_text_standard": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "f_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "The fish under the spice",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "f_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why steelhead takes to an air fryer",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "f_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Steelhead is firm enough to hold a cube through the basket without flaking apart, and fatty enough that it does not dry out at the high, dry heat an air fryer runs. That is why it crisps at the edges while the middle stays moist &mdash; a leaner white fish would be chalky by the time the outside coloured.</p><p>Ours comes from Hudson Valley, blast-frozen to -10&deg;F at harvest and vacuum sealed. Every supplier is tested before we approve them, then randomly audited to ensure consistent compliance with the Seatopia Standard &mdash; third-party lab tested for nutrition, mercury and microplastics, and sourced from best-in-class aquaculture. Farms named, panels published.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "f_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "How we source it",
            "button_link": "/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters",
            "button_style": "secondary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "f_sub",
        "f_head",
        "f_text",
        "f_btn"
      ],
